  "id": "Compound::DB00347 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Trimethadione is shown to bind to Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, and this binding is associated with participation in multiple monooxygenase activities, including (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase, (s)-limonene 6-monooxygenase, and Limonene Monooxygenase. These activities are all catalyzed by Cyp2c19, suggesting a direct interaction between Trimethadione and the Cyp2c19 enzyme. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, with Trimethadione likely acting as a substrate or inhibitor of Cyp2c9, which in turn influences the activity of Cyp2c19. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in multiple monooxygenase activities implies that Trimethadione may modulate Cyp2c19 through a common pathway, possibly by affecting the enzyme's expression or activity. The mechanistic link is supported by the observed binding and functional participation, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
